                <pb facs="0834" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115/114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Barcelona</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Barcelona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-10T21:00:00+00:00">October 10, 1936—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 11—1 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My October 8, 8 p.m. and October 9, 1 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">noon.</hi>]
                    Galvet, delegate of Industry of Catalan Department of Economy, gave assurances
                    tonight that Catalan Government would guarantee payment all cotton requisitioned
                    and would get out formal letter to that effect Monday after receiving up to date
                    list all American-owned cotton.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
